{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:claude-review@anthropic.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-06T21:03:58.787261Z","id":"8773c911ade69c06156975ba4838c7899a7e1dee800a1770a97f7e651eefc0e9","body":{"detail":"load() ends with 'figment.extract().unwrap_or_default()'. If a user has a typo in ~/.config/qualifier/config.toml or .qualifier.toml, or sets QUALIFIER_FORMAT=unknown, the extraction errors and load() silently returns Config::default(). The user has no signal that their configuration was ignored; surprising behavior. Also: load() is currently unused at the call sites I checked (no caller threads Config into commands), so this may be latent dead code, but the silence is still wrong if/when wired up.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":60},"end":{"line":60},"content_hash":"2b2f08a521620d4dd79a46b7d69d311323a0d2947dcc293738e6706dcf057f91"},"suggested_fix":"Surface extraction errors. At minimum, eprintln! a warning ('qualifier: ignoring invalid config from <source>: <err>') and return defaults. Better: return Result<Config, Error> and let run() decide whether to continue. Also worth verifying load() is actually invoked — if not, either wire it in or delete it.","summary":"figment configuration errors are silently swallowed via unwrap_or_default","tags":["review","config"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:claude-review@anthropic.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-06T21:04:04.520797Z","id":"fe7660012ad315765368de10edde22ab1f4eb42e8aac605719580760f83eb2d4","body":{"detail":"load() reads std::env::var(\"HOME\") to locate ~/.config/qualifier/config.toml. On Windows, HOME is typically unset (the analogue is USERPROFILE, and the user-config XDG-style location differs). The 'if let Ok(home)' branch is silently skipped, so Windows users cannot configure qualifier via the user-level file.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"96a6f11015c6b3a729e8f05558c7bccd797b0f0062edddf1f2e0e8a7c81f6018"},"suggested_fix":"Use the 'directories' (or 'dirs') crate's config_dir() / home_dir() to resolve the user-config path portably, falling through to USERPROFILE/HOMEDRIVE+HOMEPATH or platform APIs as that crate does. Or document that the user-level config is POSIX-only and surface an explicit warning when no home dir is found.","summary":"user-level config path uses HOME and is silently skipped on Windows","tags":["review","portability"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:claude-review@anthropic.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-06T21:04:43.911212Z","id":"c0fd1201cf8e6e1cb4e833e4a81f3c8a64b64571ffb25d9b371880af811f0345","body":{"detail":"The constant HELP_TEMPLATE renders the subcommand list (and their grouping under 'Record observations / Inspect annotations / Maintain / Other') as plain text. The Commands enum is the source of truth for parsing, but if a subcommand is added, renamed, or removed, nothing fails — the inline comment ('If you add, rename, or remove a subcommand, update HELP_TEMPLATE to match') is the only safeguard. The risk is real: 'review' is the public command name (line 30) but the source file is freshness.rs and the variant is Commands::Review wired to commands::freshness::run — a rename like that has already happened once. A future rename will silently desync the help.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":43},"content_hash":"f094e3abd8e8f1deb10ea4bdf4ca05ec5cbbd1c019ea28060f3f0563281e2c76"},"suggested_fix":"Add a unit test that parses HELP_TEMPLATE for the bullet names ('record', 'reply', 'resolve', 'emit', 'show', 'ls', 'praise', 'review', 'compact', 'haiku', 'agents') and asserts each appears as a Commands variant via clap's introspection (Cli::command().get_subcommands().map(|c| c.get_name())). The test would also catch stray entries removed from the enum but lingering in the template.","summary":"HELP_TEMPLATE manually mirrors the Commands enum with no compile-time check that they agree","tags":["review","drift-risk"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-08T03:52:20.232490Z","id":"39a16d39e1465e6dbc6b66fb37746aa26e4d9a2dc274bbafb6776f508106d305","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"load() now returns Result; cli::run validates config eagerly and exits non-zero on malformed TOML or env vars","supersedes":"8773c911ade69c06156975ba4838c7899a7e1dee800a1770a97f7e651eefc0e9"}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/config.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@empathic.dev","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-05-08T03:52:20.250956Z","id":"874345a974d314a69d7d202a9c85db88220ef5ec153ee85a5ac574232271912e","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"user-config path now falls back to USERPROFILE when HOME is unset, covering Windows","supersedes":"fe7660012ad315765368de10edde22ab1f4eb42e8aac605719580760f83eb2d4"}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/span_context.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:16:44.473325Z","id":"fdff9dc731b84a88ebff256fb51f49fde842186fa0f6b737686e69b823cf1a66","body":{"detail":"read_span_context stores file_path.display() as the header path, and show/diff pass project_root.join(subject). `qualifier show a.rs --pretty` prints `/private/tmp/.../src/a.rs:` and diff's drifted rows truncate it to `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-alex-…`, hiding the useful part; `--format json --pretty` puts the absolute path in `context.path`. Output pasted into PR descriptions (as diff.md suggests) exposes local directory layout and differs between machines.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":25},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"54d25d35a3bd6b1da27d2ac10a044f20cc3dbb4bdc6170fd4f1211bd408acfb6"},"suggested_fix":"Take a display label (the root-relative subject) separately from the filesystem path, e.g. read_span_context(path, label, span, context), and use the label in `path` and warnings.","summary":"span context headers and warnings print the absolute file path, which leaks machine paths and gets truncated in diff output","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:17:03.731225Z","id":"ee3f6adbc52fba8ac1040f723815fbee7563732227c25a9a2c9992698bb8aac5","body":{"detail":"Failure: `qualifier record concern src/a.rs:1 orig`, then `qualifier record concern lib/b.rs:1 replaces --supersedes <full id of orig>` exits 0 and writes the cross-subject supersession to lib/.qual (reproduced at ee6f8d5). SPEC and `annotation::validate_supersession_targets` (src/annotation.rs:769-789) forbid this. The check never fires because `preflight_supersession` loads only the records in the destination `.qual` (lib/.qual). `validate_supersession_targets` silently skips a target it cannot find (`if let Some(target) = by_id.get(target_id)`). `reply --supersedes` (reply.rs:131-135) has the same gap. The bad record then breaks later writes: every subsequent `record --stdin` line that supersedes anything fails with `record 28c5ea3e (subject 'lib/b.rs') supersedes d4f11b80 (subject 'src/a.rs') — cross-subject supersession is not allowed`, an error about an unrelated record, because the batch path (record.rs:413-415) validates against every record in the project.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":407},"end":{"line":415},"content_hash":"6dedafdbdfb2e8084b819aa97ff752a55a701e117287e15c4e588c1bf474b40f"},"suggested_fix":"Have the single-record paths validate against the project, as the batch path does. `require_live_id` already has the target record in hand, so compare `record.subject()` with the target's subject there (or in a shared helper), and drop the per-file `preflight_supersession`. Check only the new record's own edge so pre-existing bad records do not block unrelated writes.","summary":"preflight_supersession checks only the destination .qual file, so `record --supersedes` can supersede a record on another subject","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:17:03.731332Z","id":"029fbd321f31b9efcf566f3f601a297994c8597f11a4a94dbacfedf3d442b4d9","body":{"detail":"SPEC.md §6.10 (and site/pages/cli.md) document `issuer` and `format` keys read from `.qualifier.toml`, `~/.config/qualifier/config.toml`, and `QUALIFIER_FORMAT`. `run()` calls `config::load` only to surface parse errors and drops the result (the comment at mod.rs:117-120 says so). Issuer comes from `provenance::issuer`, which reads only the flag, `QUALIFIER_ISSUER`, and VCS. `--format` defaults to the clap literal \"human\" in every command. So `format = \"json\"` in .qualifier.toml, or `QUALIFIER_FORMAT=json`, silently does nothing. Validation still runs on these values: with `QUALIFIER_ISSUER=12345`, every command, including `qualifier haiku`, exits 1 with `invalid configuration: invalid type: found unsigned int 12345, expected a string for key \"ISSUER\"`, because figment's Env provider parses values (reproduced at ee6f8d5). provenance.rs itself would have accepted that value as a string.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":126},"content_hash":"975b923162fa4a821504b8f0f37ba31ba3ea7edeefa628da8a4961c238c0e3b0"},"suggested_fix":"Either thread Config into the commands (issuer default under QUALIFIER_ISSUER, and --format with no clap default that falls back to config.format), or remove the config keys from SPEC §6.10 and site/pages/cli.md and stop loading config. If config is kept, read QUALIFIER_* through figment as strings (for example `Env::prefixed(\"QUALIFIER_\").only(&[\"issuer\",\"format\"])` with string-typed lifting) so a numeric-looking value does not break unrelated commands.","summary":"Config is loaded and discarded: the issuer and format keys documented in SPEC §6.10 have no effect, but a bad value still fails every command","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:17:03.731414Z","id":"94e06feadb328b0dce39161fab01fd790f20b453b44cd7a46ad6d32efa236c01","body":{"detail":"`looks_like_location` returns true only when the target contains `:`, `/`, `\\`, or `.`. After `qualifier record concern Makefile mk`, running `qualifier reply Makefile hi` fails with `no record found matching prefix 'Makefile'` (reproduced at ee6f8d5). The reply/resolve help (reply.rs:57-59) promises that a `<location>` such as a file path works. The user has to know to write `./Makefile` or `Makefile:1`, and nothing in the error says so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":203},"end":{"line":213},"content_hash":"47ea70aab0b17ad34f8792c79cdd075c39dd58fb9750fceadee6d3ba6c353a13"},"suggested_fix":"Only treat a target as an ID prefix when it is all lowercase hex. Otherwise treat it as a location. When an all-hex string matches no record, fall back to the location path (or the reverse), and mention `./<name>` in the error.","summary":"reply/resolve treat an extensionless root file (Makefile, LICENSE, Dockerfile) as an ID prefix, so location targeting fails with a misleading error","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:17:03.731441Z","id":"f139beed6009b649848ae31d310411efd0ea0514043c3c42671d8e81730a0a6e","body":{"detail":"`Locator::subject` uses `strip_prefix(&self.root)`, a lexical comparison, while `root` comes from `current_dir()`, which is the physical path. On macOS, `/tmp` and `/var` are symlinks into `/private`. From a repo under /private/tmp, `qualifier record comment /tmp/.../repo/src/a.rs abs` fails with `location '/tmp/.../repo/src/a.rs' is outside the project root (/private/tmp/.../repo)` (reproduced at ee6f8d5). Tools and agents commonly pass absolute paths built from `$TMPDIR` or a symlinked checkout.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":69},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"91e8ee369c69a9a9239a66309bbfd9a6872629ed59768942795486be3afd7804"},"suggested_fix":"When the lexical strip_prefix fails, canonicalize the argument (or its longest existing ancestor, since the subject may not exist yet) and the root, then retry the strip before reporting the path as outside.","summary":"Absolute location arguments that reach the project through a symlink are rejected as outside the project root","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/provenance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:17:03.731502Z","id":"fb5d939f251ea5222d92aa2e3547e6ac663703b3c0899417d40d59ad11e64084","body":{"detail":"The module doc (provenance.rs:3-5) says each value comes from the flag, then QUALIFIER_*, then 'a detected agent harness', then VCS identity, with VCS applying to the issuer only. The --issuer help text on record, reply, resolve, and emit (for example record.rs:42) says 'defaults to QUALIFIER_ISSUER, then detected agent harness, then VCS user email'. `issuer()` (provenance.rs:46-53) goes from QUALIFIER_ISSUER straight to `detect_issuer` (VCS). Only issuer_type and session consult `HARNESSES`. Someone reading the help would expect Claude Code sessions to get a distinct issuer URI, and they do not.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":53},"content_hash":"0238e90517f16d69e141c3b7e5f99e6827b6ecce61c461303022eafbedd959e4"},"suggested_fix":"Drop 'then detected agent harness' from the --issuer help strings and reword the module doc: harness detection sets issuer_type and the session tag, and issuer comes from the flag, QUALIFIER_ISSUER, or VCS.","summary":"Docs say the issuer falls back to a detected agent harness, but provenance::issuer has no harness step","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/span_context.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:47.299654Z","id":"6356559eb8b0f6fa789a9aefaf1443a39055fd3b790736384761ab1f811d8d1e","body":{"detail":"span_context.rs:25 sets path_str = file_path.display(); callers pass project_root.join(subject) (diff.rs:593-594, show.rs:87,174). `qualifier show src/a.rs --pretty` in a scratch repo prints '/private/tmp/claude-501/.../scratchpad/vr2/src/a.rs:' above the context lines.","kind":"comment","references":"fdff9dc731b84a88ebff256fb51f49fde842186fa0f6b737686e69b823cf1a66","summary":"confirmed: span context prints the absolute filesystem path","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:19:08.965423Z","id":"6684c99996048f97cf320dbd0dbe5972bd71e2a2ba044ed1f0b2876dceac071e","body":{"detail":"In a scratch git repo built at ee6f8d5 (target/debug/qualifier): `record concern src/a.rs:1 orig`, then `record concern lib/b.rs:1 replaces --supersedes <orig id>` exited 0. A later unrelated stdin line `{\"kind\":\"concern\",\"location\":\"src/a.rs:2\",\"supersedes\":\"<live src/a.rs id>\"}` failed with `record 60840c49 (subject 'lib/b.rs') supersedes 0d005fef (subject 'src/a.rs') — cross-subject supersession is not allowed`. Cause: preflight_supersession (src/cli/targets.rs:413-420) loads only the destination .qual, and validate_supersession_targets skips unknown targets (src/annotation.rs:775 `if let Some(target) = by_id.get(target_id)`). reply.rs:133-134 uses the same preflight.","kind":"comment","references":"ee3f6adbc52fba8ac1040f723815fbee7563732227c25a9a2c9992698bb8aac5","summary":"confirmed: record --supersedes across subjects is accepted and then poisons later batch writes","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:19:08.965461Z","id":"0e132e43ecec9889315b49a873c6420fca0d1e5148905045aa1cbf98dbb61a71","body":{"detail":"src/cli/mod.rs:117-125 calls config::load and discards the result. In a scratch git repo built at ee6f8d5 (target/debug/qualifier): `QUALIFIER_ISSUER=12345 qualifier haiku` exited 1 with `invalid configuration: invalid type: found unsigned int 12345, expected a string for key \"ISSUER\"`; `QUALIFIER_FORMAT=json qualifier record comment src/a.rs fmt` printed human output; with .qualifier.toml `format = \"json\"` and `issuer = \"mailto:cfg@x\"`, record printed human output and stored issuer mailto:alex@kesling.co (VCS). SPEC.md:1196-1214 documents both keys.","kind":"comment","references":"029fbd321f31b9efcf566f3f601a297994c8597f11a4a94dbacfedf3d442b4d9","summary":"confirmed: config is loaded only for validation; SPEC 6.10 keys have no effect but bad values fail every command","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:19:08.965485Z","id":"10a6bdde0fd2c4ab9483d1c19ed5986ef1cd1b989d150ab3a72dc0cee19d1ef1","body":{"detail":"In a scratch git repo built at ee6f8d5 (target/debug/qualifier): `record concern Makefile mk`, then `reply Makefile hi` exited 1 with `no record found matching prefix 'Makefile'`. looks_like_location (src/cli/targets.rs:203-213) returns false for a string with no ':', '/', '\\\\' or '.', so resolve_target (218-230) calls resolve_id_prefix.","kind":"comment","references":"94e06feadb328b0dce39161fab01fd790f20b453b44cd7a46ad6d32efa236c01","summary":"confirmed: extensionless root file names are treated as ID prefixes by reply/resolve","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:19:08.965495Z","id":"f5574c342fb85801f1d2180ff9f91134b231e8cbcd106e39b774f20bb98f4d1d","body":{"detail":"In a scratch git repo built at ee6f8d5 (target/debug/qualifier) under /private/tmp: `record comment /tmp/.../repo/src/a.rs abs` exited 1 with `location '/tmp/.../repo/src/a.rs' is outside the project root (/private/tmp/.../repo)`. Locator::subject (src/cli/targets.rs:70-73) uses lexical path.strip_prefix(&self.root), and root comes from current_dir() (targets.rs:41-42), which is the physical path.","kind":"comment","references":"f139beed6009b649848ae31d310411efd0ea0514043c3c42671d8e81730a0a6e","summary":"confirmed: absolute paths through a symlinked prefix are rejected as outside the root","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/provenance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:19:08.965519Z","id":"049ff7ab383b9267d33758cbe919f3adf1df525bcbde2ec33e8bb51138fdd98b","body":{"detail":"src/cli/commands/record.rs:42 help says `defaults to QUALIFIER_ISSUER, then detected agent harness, then VCS user email`; src/cli/provenance.rs:3-5 lists a harness step. issuer() at provenance.rs:46-53 is explicit -> env_nonempty(QUALIFIER_ISSUER) -> detect_issuer (VCS); detected_harness() is not called there. In this session (CLAUDECODE=1) records got issuer mailto:alex@kesling.co from VCS.","kind":"comment","references":"fb5d939f251ea5222d92aa2e3547e6ac663703b3c0899417d40d59ad11e64084","summary":"confirmed: --issuer help and module doc claim a harness step that issuer() does not have","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212410Z","id":"8fb57bc7e197fcb9094fb817f620773b4ad03bf452257c9e1d41ef091d5ca140","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/cli/mod.rs:22-43 lists init/threads/diff, which the Commands enum defines at mod.rs:70,87,96; no test references HELP_TEMPLATE (`grep -rn HELP_TEMPLATE src tests` finds only mod.rs:13,15,60)","kind":"comment","references":"c0fd1201cf8e6e1cb4e833e4a81f3c8a64b64571ffb25d9b371880af811f0345","summary":"Resolution: Still unguarded (src/cli/mod.rs:10-14 still relies on a comment). Add a unit test in src/cli/mod.rs that pulls the two-space-indented command names out of HELP_TEMPLATE and compares them as a set with Cli::command().get_subcommands().map(|c| c.get_name()) plus 'help'. The test's name list must come from parsing the template, not a hardcoded list: the one in the suggested fix is already stale and lacks init, threads and diff.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/provenance.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212419Z","id":"651e4fbd1bb9ddc38321268fb6447a075727090f76c03adcaf365d6263815c54","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/cli/provenance.rs:46-53 issuer() goes from the explicit flag to env QUALIFIER_ISSUER to detect_issuer, with no detected_harness() call","kind":"comment","references":"fb5d939f251ea5222d92aa2e3547e6ac663703b3c0899417d40d59ad11e64084","summary":"Resolution: Confirmed. Remove 'then detected agent harness' from the --issuer help on record (record.rs:42), reply, resolve and emit. Reword the doc at src/cli/provenance.rs:3-5 to say: harness detection sets issuer_type and the session tag; issuer comes from the flag, then QUALIFIER_ISSUER, then VCS.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212428Z","id":"6df077545b25762c543422d4a40d07475624ef6a3a748a67d821348c7aa50819","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/cli/targets.rs:70-73 uses path.strip_prefix(&self.root), while root comes from current_dir() (targets.rs:41-42); confirming reply: a /tmp/... path was rejected against root /private/tmp/...","kind":"comment","references":"f139beed6009b649848ae31d310411efd0ea0514043c3c42671d8e81730a0a6e","summary":"Resolution: Confirmed. In Locator::subject (src/cli/targets.rs:69-76), when the lexical strip_prefix fails, canonicalize the root and the argument's longest existing ancestor, then retry strip_prefix and re-append the part that does not exist yet. Report 'outside the project root' only if that also fails.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212437Z","id":"0b51971b9da23f2a0eb406c9856ba5499cb97952eeb9d61ed6e5c2970a847706","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/cli/targets.rs:203-213 returns false for a string with no ':', '/', '\\\\' or '.'; confirming reply: `reply Makefile hi` failed with `no record found matching prefix 'Makefile'`","kind":"comment","references":"94e06feadb328b0dce39161fab01fd790f20b453b44cd7a46ad6d32efa236c01","summary":"Resolution: Confirmed. In looks_like_location/resolve_target (src/cli/targets.rs:203-230), treat a target as an ID prefix only when it is all lowercase hex; treat anything else as a location. If an all-hex target matches no record, try it as a location, and add a hint to try `./<name>` in the error.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/targets.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212445Z","id":"c9169715f3afd1da35cb43fdaf07b68466d9a91631c20c6c4be570442555335c","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/annotation.rs:775 `if let Some(target) = by_id.get(target_id)` skips unknown targets; confirming reply: a cross-subject `record --supersedes` exited 0, then a later unrelated batch line failed","kind":"comment","references":"ee3f6adbc52fba8ac1040f723815fbee7563732227c25a9a2c9992698bb8aac5","summary":"Resolution: Confirmed. In the single-record paths (record.rs run(), reply.rs:131-135), check that the target subject equals record.subject() inside require_live_id, which already has the target record. Then remove preflight_supersession (src/cli/targets.rs:407-420). Validate only the new record's own edge so existing bad records do not block unrelated writes. Also make validate_supersession_targets (src/annotation.rs:775) return an error for unknown targets, not skip them.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/span_context.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212587Z","id":"b936cc090f1ad4d6c6a97c523221c172270ffce9799c09171db9960cb2dfef9d","body":{"detail":"Evidence: src/cli/span_context.rs:26 (`let path_str = file_path.display().to_string()` is used as the header path); callers pass project_root.join(subject) at src/cli/commands/diff.rs:594","kind":"comment","references":"fdff9dc731b84a88ebff256fb51f49fde842186fa0f6b737686e69b823cf1a66","summary":"Resolution: Change read_span_context(file_path, span, context) at span_context.rs:25 to also take a display label (the root-relative subject). Use the label for SpanContext.path and in warnings, and keep file_path for reading. Pass &att.subject or &subject from diff.rs:593-594 and show.rs:87,174.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:34:02.796792Z","id":"848d3c4918669e77a1f9739120220b9b356032e1209c41f8ecee3ddeefe9ef25","body":{"detail":"Option A: thread Config into the commands (issuer default after QUALIFIER_ISSUER; --format falls back to config.format; read QUALIFIER_* as strings so numeric values stop breaking every command). Adds surface, minor version bump. Option B: remove the issuer/format keys from SPEC.md:1196-1214 and site/pages/cli.md, document the env vars that do work (QUALIFIER_ISSUER, QUALIFIER_ISSUER_TYPE, QUALIFIER_SESSION), and stop calling config::load (src/cli/mod.rs:117-125). Recommendation: B; no command consumes Config today, and removing it also removes the numeric-env crash. Also covers the duplicate SPEC thread dcef24fc.","kind":"comment","references":"029fbd321f31b9efcf566f3f601a297994c8597f11a4a94dbacfedf3d442b4d9","summary":"Needs a decision: Should the config file drive defaults, or be removed from the spec?","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"src/cli/mod.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"human","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:38:00.579111Z","id":"d683a650b080184288b0f3abdc964e69881c3222a54a933e2c56f4694d5fd319","body":{"detail":"Wire it in","kind":"comment","references":"029fbd321f31b9efcf566f3f601a297994c8597f11a4a94dbacfedf3d442b4d9","summary":"Decided: wire Config in. A committed .qualifier.toml (and user config) supplies issuer and format defaults below CLI flags and env vars, as SPEC §6.10 describes; QUALIFIER_* values are read as strings so non-string-looking values no longer fail every command.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
